This leads me to a crucial question: is the "Spring Boot" in the `pom.xml` actually the official Spring Boot from `https://spring.io/projects/spring-boot`, or is it a custom framework 
built *on top* of Spring? The irregular version numbers (Spring Boot 4.0.6, Spring Core 7.0.7) strongly point towards the latter.

Considering the overarching goal to "Preserve existing application behavior," I must exercise extreme caution before attempting a direct upgrade of the `spring-boot-starter-parent`. 
