Reasoning:
Alright, so I've been reviewing the build output, and it looks like `mvn verify`
has thrown a compilation error within `task-web`, specifically in the 
`TaskApplicationTest.java` file. The specific issue is that it's complaining 
about missing `org.junit.jupiter.api` and 
`org.springframework.boot.test.context` packages, and it can't resolve the 
`SpringBootTest` and `Test` annotations.

Now, I know exactly why this is happening. When I was working on migrating the 
logging configuration to use Log4j, I must have inadvertently removed the 
`spring-boot-starter-test` dependency. This starter is crucial because it's what
pulls in JUnit 5 (Jupiter, as the errors suggest) and all the necessary Spring 
Boot testing annotations.

I've just checked the current `task-web/pom.xml`, specifically lines 50 through 
71 where the dependencies are declared, and sure enough, the 
`spring-boot-starter-test` dependency is nowhere to be found in that section.

So, the fix is straightforward: I need to re-insert the 
`spring-boot-starter-test` dependency into `task-web/pom.xml`. I'll make sure to
define it with the `test` scope, and I'll place it right after the 
`log4j-to-slf4j` dependency, just before the closing `</dependencies>` tag. That
should bring back the required JUnit and Spring Boot testing components.

